<title>LITHUANIA: VILNIAUS BANK SIGNS 2.2 MILLION DM LOAN.</title>
<headline>VILNIAUS BANK SIGNS 2.2 MILLION DM LOAN.</headline>
<dateline>VILNIUS 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Leading Lithuanian commercial bank Vilniaus bank said on Tuesday that it had signed a loan worth 2.2 million German marks with Germany's Schleswig-Holstein Girozentrale.</p>
<p>The bank said in a statement that the loan was its first medium-term direct inter-banking loan.</p>
<p>The term of the loan is for three years. The bank did not give the conditions for the loan.</p>
<p>--Ed Stoddard, Vilnius newsroom +370 2 22 35 17</p>
</text>
